{"url": "https://www.strath.ac.uk/science/physics/internationalstudents/internationaladmissions/", "final_url": "https://www.strath.ac.uk/science/physics/internationalstudents/internationaladmissions/", "status": 200, "method": "http", "fetched": "2026-10-26", "text": "International admissions | University of Strathclyde\nSkip to content\nStudy with us\nStudy with us\nCourse search\nUndergraduate\nPostgraduate taught\nPostgraduate research\nPostgraduate research & PhD opportunities\nUniversity of Strathclyde, Bahrain\nApprenticeship Degrees\nStrathclyde Online Learning\nScholarships\nAccommodation\nInternational students\nCentre for Lifelong Learning\nStudy abroad\nWork with us\nWork with us\nResearch\nJob vacancies\nStaff search\nTraining & consultancy\nConferencing & events\nInnovation & industry engagement\nWhy Strathclyde?\nWhy Strathclyde?\nOur campus\nEmployability\nGlasgow\nScotland\nStrathclyde Sport\nNews\nUniversity governance\nAccess to information\nCurrent students\nA-Z Guide\nEmail\nMyPlace\nLibrary\nStrathclyde Sport\nCareers\nSafe360\nStrath Union\nPegasus\nTell Strathclyde\nStaff\nEmail\nPegasus\nTelephone Directory\nSafe360\niTrent\nWebsite search\nScience\nPhysics\nInternational students\nInternational admissions\nPhysicsInternational admissions\nThe University of Strathclyde welcomes students from many countries. Visit our international students' section for country specific information, and full details of entry requirements.\nWe provide foundation programmes for preparatory studies for both prospective undergraduate and postgraduate students.\nLanguage requirements\nIn all cases, applicants whose first language is not English must show an appropriate level of competence in the English language. For the Department of Physics this is deemed to be IELTS (academic) at 6.0.\nTo satisfy UK Visas and Immigration requirements, no element of IELTS should be below 5.5. If you require information about other English language qualifications then please contact the department.\nThe University's English Language Teaching department offers pre-entry and pre-sessional courses for new international students from April each year. Full fee paying students are entitled to one month of pre-sessional English course free of charge.\nDirect entry to our undergraduate degrees\nIt's possible for suitably qualified candidates to gain direct entry to a later year of the MPhys or BSc degrees. If you have previously studied physics or a related subject at university level in another country, you may be eligible to enrol directly into Year 2, 3 or 4 of the MPhys or BSc degree, depending on your previous qualifications.\nWe have articulation agreements with SNU and Donghua University which allow their students to join us from year 3.\nTo assist us in determining your year of entry, you should send us a copy of your transcript in English. If you have any queries relating to direct entry to any of our courses please contact us.\nUndergraduate applications\nIf you have just left school and are seeking first year entry you should contact your local British Council Office to find out whether your school-leaving qualifications are sufficient.\nContact Physics\n+44 (0) 141 548 3366\nphysics-study-enquiries@strath.ac.uk\nOur location\nFind a member of our staff\nLike us on Facebook\nFollow us on Instagram\nConnect with us on Linkedin\nHow to Apply\nUndergraduate\nApply for an undergraduate course\nPostgraduate Taught\nApply for a postgraduate taught course\nPostgraduate Research\nApply for a postgraduate research course\nRelated Information\nInternational Students - Physics\nAcademic Admission requirements\nFees, scholarships & cost of living\nEntry visa information\nDiscover our City\nYour place in our community\nInternational Student Support Team\nOur graduates\nBack to top\nOur faculties & departments\nEngineering\nFaculty of Engineering\nArchitecture\nBiomedical Engineering\nChemical & Process Engineering\nCivil & Environmental Engineering\n